    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the most elegant way to descend... that's a heavy way to put it. it's almost like you're suggesting that there's a kind of grace in just letting go instead of struggling. like, instead of fighting the bankruptcy and the loss and the failure, there's a way to finish it with some dignity? that it's actually more logical to just accept the end of the trajectory than to keep trying to climb back up a hill that doesn't exist.",
